      "extract": "Deﬁnition 2.8. Let W be a Coxeter group. An element w is said to be fully commutative if any reduced word for w can be obtained from any other by interchange of adjacent commuting generators. Stembridge [16] classiﬁed all of the Coxeter groups that have ﬁnitely many fully commutative elements. His results completed the work of Fan [5], who had done this for the simply-laced types. In the same paper [5], Fan showed",
